        "event": "Flood Watch",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued June 1 at 3:39PM AKDT until June 3 at 10:00AM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
        "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Kodiak Island, including the communities of Kodiak City,\nPort Lions, Ouzinkie, Old Harbor.\n\n* WHEN...Through Wednesday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff from heavy rain may result in flooding\nof rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations, including Bells Flats. Heavy rain may saturate soils,\nresulting in isolated landslides in areas of steep terrain. Strong\neast to northeast winds",
        "severity": "Severe",
        "certainty": "Possible",
        "urgency": "Future",
        "sender": "NWS Anchorage AK",
        "effective": "2026-06-01T15:39:00-08:00",
        "expires": "2026-06-03T10:00:00-08:00",
        "areas": "Kodiak Island Northeast; Kodiak Island Southwest",
        "category": "Met",
        "response": "Prepare",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.\n\nStay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further informat",
        "lat": null,
        "lng": null
      },
      {
